`local` is not a weights kind. There are three -- `digest`, `hosted` and
`canned` -- and they are three because each decides something different about
what a result may claim: a digest can be re-fired, hosted weights can change
under a re-firing, and a canned server has no weights at all.

A fourth kind read as "close enough to a digest" would be identity by guess.
The vocabulary is closed, so a reader that meets one it does not know says so
instead of picking.

This reason said TWO until 2026-09-12. `canned` was added by `fc70015` in this
same PR, on the 2026-09-11 ruling, and that commit updated other `.reason`
files and not this one. Nothing in the gate compares a `.reason` to the tree
-- it is read only when its fixture unexpectedly parses -- so a fixture can go
on refusing correctly while the text beside it teaches a vocabulary that has
grown. Found by a fresh instance reading the two against each other.
